# ============================================================
# 🧠 CONCEPT: Frontend env vars are PUBLIC and BAKED IN AT BUILD TIME
# WHY IT MATTERS (interview angle): two differences from the backend that
#   matter a lot:
#   1. ⚠️ NOTHING HERE IS SECRET. Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into
#      the JavaScript bundle at build time, and every visitor downloads
#      that bundle. Putting an API key, a database URL, or a private token
#      in here publishes it. This has leaked a lot of credentials in real
#      projects. If a value must stay secret, it belongs on the SERVER,
#      with the frontend calling an endpoint that uses it.
#   2. Values are substituted AT BUILD TIME, not read at runtime. So one
#      built artifact cannot serve staging and production with different
#      API URLs — you build per environment, or fetch config at runtime
#      from something like /config.json.
#
#   Only variables PREFIXED WITH VITE_ are exposed to client code. That
#   prefix requirement is a deliberate guard so that a stray AWS_SECRET in
#   your shell environment is not accidentally bundled.
# ============================================================

# Not needed for local development — vite.config.js proxies /api to
# localhost:5000, which also avoids CORS entirely. Set this only if you
# point the client at a deployed API on a different origin.
VITE_API_URL=/api
